0221: Inkling 2 Mini's loop controller (the loop model's message merge, src/models/inkling2.cpp control()) as one op, GGML_OP_LOOP_CONTROL (appended after GGML_OP_GATED_DELTA_NET_REPLAY, so every earlier op keeps its id), behind GGML_OPENCL_LOOP_CONTROL (unset, 0, off: nothing changes, the chain is emitted node for node; 1 or f32: the f32 kernel; bf16: the bf16-DPAS build of the same kernel; all-layers: 1 and the layer guard lifted; any other value: off, with a WARN line). The op: ggml.h/ggml.c (constructor, a pure rule ggml_loop_control_refuse, the knob's parser, a pure launch plan ggml_loop_control_plan_make shared with the host replay), a CPU reference that is the unfused chain in f32 (ops.cpp), and one OpenCL kernel kernel_loop_control (loop_control.cl): a work-group of 32 sub-groups a Xe core, phase A the down product with the two norms folded in as scales after it (g in local memory, K-split partials reduced in local memory), phase B the gain and forget products, tanh and the combine in registers, out the only global write; the next block's loads issued before the current block computes, prefetches where the ISA shows the loads sunk to their use; 256 GRF, no spill on bmg-g21 / bmg-g31 (both maths). The model emits the op for prompt batches (more than 8 rows) on a layer whose backend declares it (get_proc_address "ggml_backend_loop_control", the FA port's layer guard), else the chain with one DOWNGRADE line; an adapter, a Hadamard rotation or a precision entry on a controller weight keeps the chain. The trailing rms_norm stays a node. Reds through GGML_OPENCL_LOOP_CONTROL_OPTS=-DLOOP_CONTROL_RED=1..5; GGML_OPENCL_LOOP_CONTROL_STATS=1 prints the launches a graph; bounds always checked before the launch. test-backend-ops: LOOP_CONTROL cases at 1 .. 1,027 rows (plain and a mix column's view), the twin against the unfused chain on the same backend, perf cases op against chain.

